          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em quantum anomalous Hall effect
            (QAHE) is a joint variant of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+effect"} quantum Hall effect
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+Hall+effect"} anomalous Hall effect
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+effect"} quantum Hall effect
            is induced by a strong
            %em external
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crystal"} crystalline
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+phases+of+matter"} topological phases of matter
            called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+insulators"} Chern insulators
            — the effect of the external magnetic field on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            is instead mimicked by the latter’s
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin-orbit+coupling"} spin-orbit coupling
            in the presence of magnetization, jointly reflected in a non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+curvature"} Berry curvature
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brillouin+torus"} Brillouin torus
            which now plays the role of the external field’s
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flux+density"} flux density
          %p
            In analogy to how the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+effect"} quantum Hall effect
            has a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "quantum+Hall+effect#IdeaFQHE"} fractional version
            %em fractional quantum anomalous Hall effect
            (FQAHE).
          %h2#details Details
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -60px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/ChangLiuMacDonald2023-Fig1.png", :width => "400px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                (from
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#ChangLiuMacDonald23"} Chang, Liu, MacDonald 2023
          %blockquote
            %p
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "#ChangLiuMacDonald23"}> Chang, Liu &amp; MacDonald 2023 §II.A
              \:&amp;rbrack; A common feature of all the QAH systems that are established as of this writing — magnetically doped
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} TI
              films, films of the intrinsic magnetic TI
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Mn
                      %msub
                        %mi Bi
                        %mn 2
                      %msub
                        %mi Te
                        %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Mn Bi_2 Te_4
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphene"} graphene
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mtext -
                      %mi BN
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h\text{-}BN
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+equations"} Dirac equations
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi D
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (m/\hbar v_D)^2
              (where
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi D
                      %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %mi x
                      %mo ∼
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mrow
                          %mi D
                          %mo ,
                          %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_D \sim v_{D,x} \sim v_{D,y}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \mathbf{k} \vert}^{-3}
              for large
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\vert \mathbf{k} \vert}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm (e^2/2 h)
              to the Hall conductivity
          %p#FQAHDetails
            Moreover, for fractional quantum Hall systems the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+band"} valence band
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                is “almost flat”, meaning that its energy gradient with respect to momentum is small, so that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+energy"} kinetic energy
                of electrons is small (“quenched”) and the electron-interaction/correlation is dominant
            %li
              %p overlaps the Fermi energy, so that it is only partially (fractionally) filled, with holes at the peaks of the Dirac domes:
          %div{:style => "margin: -30px 0px 20px 30px"}
            %img{:src => "/nlab/files/FQAH-BandStructure.png", :width => "640px"}/
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
          %p
            %strong Types of Hall effects
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hall+effect"}> Hall effect
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anomalous+Hall+effect"} anomalous Hall effect
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+Hall+effect"}> quantum Hall effect
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+anomalous+Hall+effect"} quantum anomalous Hall effect
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+spin+Hall+effect"} quantum
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+Hall+effect"} spin Hall effect
          %h2#references References
          %h3#integer_qahe Integer QAHE
          %p
            The theoretical prediction of Hall conductance proportional to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+number"} first Chern number
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral"} integrated
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+curvature"} Berry curvature
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/valence+band"} valence band
            in a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulator"} topological insulator
          %ul
            %li
              D. J. Thouless, M. Kohmoto, M. P. Nightingale, M. den Nijs:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantized Hall Conductance in a Two-Dimensional Periodic Potential
              %strong 49
              (1982) 405 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.49.405"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.49.405
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The first theoretical lattice model, which came to be called the
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Haldane+model"} Haldane model
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Duncan+Haldane"}> Duncan Haldane
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Model for a Quantum Hall Effect without Landau Levels: Condensed-Matter Realization of the “Parity Anomaly”
              %strong 61
              (1988) 2015 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.61.2015"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.61.2015
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Experimental realization of QAH systems:
          %ul
            %li
              Cui-Zu Chang et al.:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Experimental Observation of the Quantum Anomalous Hall Effect in a Magnetic Topological Insulator
              %strong 340
              (2013) 167 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1234414"}> doi:10.1126/science.1234414
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.08829"} arXiv:1605.08829
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Jing Wang,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Biao+Lian"} Biao Lian
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shou-Cheng+Zhang"} Shou-Cheng Zhang
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum anomalous Hall effect in magnetic topological insulators
                %strong 2015
                T164 (2015) 014003 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.6715"}> arXiv:1409.6715
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/0031-8949/2015/T164/014003"} doi:10.1088/0031-8949/2015/T164/014003
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chao-Xing+Liu"}> Chao-Xing Liu
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shou-Cheng+Zhang"} Shou-Cheng Zhang
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Quantum Anomalous Hall Effect: Theory and Experiment
                %strong 7
                (2016) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.07106"}> arXiv:1508.07106
                ,
